This file is NOT a native addon. It is a placeholder with a .node extension, placed at the
canonical node-gyp output path (build/Release/) so capwall's native-addon load gate (#49) can
be exercised without a compiler in CI.

The gate runs BEFORE process.dlopen touches the file, so a denial is observable with this file
exactly as it would be with a real addon. When the gate ALLOWS the load, dlopen is reached and
fails with the platform's own "not a valid ELF/Mach-O/PE" error — which is precisely how
test/native.test.ts distinguishes "gate fired" (CapabilityError) from "gate passed" (a real
loader error). A genuinely loadable addon is additionally borrowed from the installed
dependency tree when one is present; see findRealAddon() in that file.
